items.test:
apps/mobile/src/screens/match/__tests__/goHandoff.test.tsx (5 tests), rewritten as the reviewer asked:
- The game stand-in now does exactly what app/game.tsx does: useState(handedGoCover), `useEffect(() => handGoCover(null), [])`, and `<Stack.Screen options={{ gestureEnabled: false }} />` on every render.
- The match stand-in does what app/match/index.tsx does: handGoCover, push, dropWhenCovered.
- On the real expo-router native stack, after the GO! press:
  - the handoff is already cleared;
  - 3 RNSScreens remain, and the match screen's GO! is still in the tree;
  - the game's RNSScreen has stackAnimation 'none' after its effects and setOptions;
  - firing the match screen's onDisappear drops it (2 screens left), the game keeps 'none', and back goes Home;
  - a later plain push to /game gets 'fade'.
- Unit test: the cut is sticky per key after handGoCover(null), and other keys get the flow, with Reduced Motion off and on.
- Source pins: the layout passes `route.key`; the match route pushes, then calls dropWhenCovered, and never replaces /game.
- The react-native-screens source facts it relies on are pinned too.
Fails on the old code: with the non-sticky handed-based transition swapped back in, 3 of 5 tests fail, including 'Expected "none", Received "fade"' (the reviewer's finding). Restored afterwards.
